   189	operation and identity across operations; it does not prove upstream
   190	authenticity, and v1 verifies no toolchain signature.
   191	
   192	## 4. Ordering
   193	
   194	### 4.1 Stage A — availability, version, platform
   195	
   196	Runs immediately after manifest parsing and build-command validation
   197	(`profiles/manager.md` section 2.1 phase 4), for every distinct toolchain in
   198	the plan, in Unicode-scalar lexical order of toolchain identifier, once per
   199	operation, memoized only in operation-private state. For each toolchain:
   200	
   201	1. compute the effective requirement from registry baseline, manifest, and
   202	   descriptor sources available at this point, rejecting an empty intersection;
   203	2. resolve the root from an admissible origin only and verify the primary
   204	   executable is a regular executable at `primary_relpath`;
   205	3. run the entry probe from a manager-owned empty working directory under the
   206	   operation-private environment;
   207	4. normalize to the canonical triple and reject a prerelease;
   208	5. verify the host `(operating_system, architecture)` is in `platforms` and
   209	   that the toolchain's own reported host target equals the manager's native
   210	   target — cross-compilation stays forbidden;
   211	6. evaluate the effective requirement.
