   221	A descriptor requirement is not readable at Stage A for an external command,
   222	because the descriptor arrives with the repository. Stage A therefore gates on
   223	baseline ∩ manifest, and the descriptor requirement joins the intersection at
   224	Stage B. This is the only ordering asymmetry and it is deliberate: the
   225	consuming manifest requirement is REQUIRED precisely so the cheap gate always
   226	has something to evaluate.
   227	
   228	Failure of any toolchain in the plan fails the operation. Partial installation
   229	of a closure is already forbidden by the journal and rollback rules.
   230	
   231	### 4.2 Stage B — source-metadata cross-check
   232	
   233	Runs per active build command after local snapshot validation, or after exact
   234	external acquisition and audit (`profiles/manager.md` section 11.6 steps 1
   235	through 6), and before the manager reads an artifact-cache candidate or starts
   236	a compiler child. It re-evaluates the effective requirement including any
   237	descriptor requirement, then applies the entry's metadata rules.
   238	
   239	Metadata is an assertion about the already-resolved toolchain. It never
   240	selects, downloads, activates, switches, or re-resolves anything.
   241	
   242	| Toolchain | Rule |
   243	|---|---|
   244	| `go` | `go.mod` `go` directive above resolved → mismatch. `toolchain` directive above resolved → mismatch; at or below resolved → permitted and never honored, consistent with `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`. |
   245	| `rust` | `rust-version` above resolved → mismatch. `rust-toolchain.toml` `channel` above resolved → mismatch; `stable`, `beta`, `nightly`, or a dated channel → mismatch. `components`, `targets`, `profile` ignored. `path` → package influence. |
   246	| `swift` | `// swift-tools-version:` above resolved → mismatch. `.swift-version` above resolved, or naming a snapshot → mismatch. |
   247	| `kotlin` | the single selected file and field, same shape. |
   248	
   249	Across all languages, metadata naming an executable path, URL, mirror,
   250	registry, credential, or install command is
   251	`build_toolchain_package_influence_forbidden`.
   252	
   253	### 4.3 Cache, dry-run, status
   254	
   255	Neither stage may be skipped by a cache hit, a dry run, or an offline mode. A
   256	cache hit is only reachable after Stage A and Stage B pass, so no hit can
   257	bypass a requirement.
   258	
   259	Dry-run runs both stages — neither needs a compiler or a mutation — and reports
   260	an affected command as `blocked` with the typed diagnostic, returning failure
   261	and leaving no mutation. `blocked` therefore joins the local dry-run vocabulary
   262	of section 2.4, matching section 11.7. `unsupported` continues to mean an
   263	unknown driver and MUST NOT be reused for a toolchain failure.
   264	
   265	Read-only status and audit report a Stage A or Stage B failure as a finding and
   266	MUST NOT mark an otherwise valid marker non-current because of it. Install,
   267	upgrade, repair, and coverage-claiming audit fail before mutation.
   268	
   269	## 5. Diagnostics
   270	
   271	| Code | Stage | Trigger |
   272	|---|---|---|
   273	| `build_toolchain_requirement_invalid` | validation | malformed object, unknown identifier, identifier not the driver's primary, bad literal, prerelease literal, `min` not below `below` |
   274	| `build_toolchain_requirement_unsatisfiable` | validation | empty intersection of baseline, manifest, and descriptor requirements |
   275	| `build_toolchain_unavailable` | A | no trusted toolchain configured or resolvable for the identifier |
   276	| `build_toolchain_untrusted` | A | forbidden origin, wrapper or shim, primary executable outside the fingerprinted tree, not a regular executable, or unprotected configuration state |
   277	| `build_toolchain_version_undetermined` | A | probe output unbounded, unmatched, or ambiguous |
   278	| `build_toolchain_prerelease_unsupported` | A | resolved toolchain is a prerelease, nightly, beta, or development snapshot |
   279	| `build_toolchain_platform_unsupported` | A | host pair outside `platforms`, or reported host target differs from the native target |
   280	| `build_toolchain_incompatible` | A | resolved release version outside the effective requirement |
   281	| `build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch` | B | declared source metadata incompatible with the resolved toolchain |
   282	| `build_toolchain_package_influence_forbidden` | validation, A, B | manifest, descriptor, or metadata supplies a path, URL, mirror, channel, command, environment override, credential, or trust root |
   283	| `build_toolchain_changed` | A, publication | resolved identity or version changed during the operation |
   284	
   285	Every code is stable, carries the toolchain identifier, the effective
   286	requirement, the resolved version when known, and a `guidance_id`. A code MUST
   287	NOT carry prose guidance or a URL of its own.
   288	
   289	## 6. `toolchain-guidance-catalog-v1`
   290	
   291	Manager-owned and versioned. Each entry is
   292	`{guidance_id, toolchain_id, reason, platform, primary_source, summary}` and
   293	`superseded_by` when retired.
   294	
   295	`guidance_id` grammar: `toolchain.<toolchain_id>.<reason>.<platform>`, where
   296	`platform` is `linux`, `macos`, `windows`, or `any`.
   297	
   298	Guidance-carrying reasons: `unavailable`, `incompatible`,
   299	`prerelease_unsupported`, `platform_unsupported`, `untrusted`,
   300	`metadata_mismatch`.
   301	
   302	Selection is exact `(toolchain_id, reason, platform)`, then the `any` platform.
   303	The catalog MUST be total over supported toolchains × guidance-carrying reasons
   304	× supported platforms, enforced by a release gate, so no runtime
   305	guidance-missing case exists.
   306	
   307	`primary_source` MUST be the language's own official origin — never a package,
   308	a mirror, a third-party installer script, or a command the manager runs.
   309	Guidance is text plus URL only.
   310	
   311	Lifecycle: append-only within a catalog version; any change of meaning or of
   312	`primary_source` origin requires a new `guidance_id`; retirement sets
   313	`superseded_by`; the catalog version advances with the specification release.
   314	The catalog is not a cache, receipt, marker, or claim input, so correcting a
   315	URL never invalidates an artifact.
   316	
   317	`TASK-260728-ypbuav` owns catalog maintenance.
   318	
   319	## 7. No auto-install
   320	
   321	v1 never downloads, installs, updates, activates, or switches a toolchain, and
   322	specifically not through `rustup`, `swiftly`, `sdkman`, `asdf`, `mise`,
   323	Homebrew, `winget`, the Gradle wrapper, or `GOTOOLCHAIN`. A missing or
   324	incompatible toolchain is an installation error with a typed code and a
   325	guidance identifier. Introducing auto-install requires a new decision, a new
   326	trust model for installer code, and its own review.
   327	
   328	## 8. Vector inventory
   329	
   330	`TASK-260728-2jaw7h` MUST land at least these cases.

