   104	## 2. `toolchain-requirement-v1`
   105	
   106	### 2.1 Canonical version
   107	
   108	A canonical version is `major.minor.patch`, matching
   109	`^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$` with each component at
   110	most `999999`. No `v`, `go`, or `swift-` prefix, no prerelease, no build
   111	metadata, no leading zeros, no wildcard. Order is lexicographic over the triple.
   112	
   113	### 2.2 Requirement object
   114	
   115	```json
   116	{"id": "go", "version": {"kind": "at_least", "min": "1.23.0"}}
   117	{"id": "go", "version": {"kind": "range", "min": "1.23.0", "below": "1.25.0"}}
   118	{"id": "go", "version": {"kind": "exact", "equals": "1.23.4"}}
   119	```
   120	
   121	`toolchain` contains exactly `id` and `version`. `version` contains exactly
   122	`kind` plus that kind's own fields. `id` MUST equal the driver's registry
   123	primary toolchain; a mismatch is `build_toolchain_requirement_invalid`. For
   124	`range`, `min` MUST be strictly below `below`.
