   102	### 2.2 Closed `go-v1` toolchain and process graph
   103	
   104	A conforming manager MUST support an operator-trusted Go 1.23 release family
   105	that it has tested against the `go-v1` conformance vectors. It MAY allowlist
   106	additional Go release families only after testing those families against the
   107	same vectors. It MUST reject a pre-1.23, malformed, package-selected, or
   108	otherwise unknown release, including a newer release merely ordered after a
   109	known one. The launcher is selected independently of the package and MUST be
   110	the regular executable `<GOROOT>/bin/go` (`bin/go.exe` on Windows), never a
   111	wrapper, repository file, runtime command, project shim, manifest value, or
   112	executable found through the user `PATH`.
   113	
   114	Before entering a package-controlled directory, the manager creates an
   115	operation-private probe root. From a manager-owned empty working directory it
   116	invokes the resolved `go` executable directly with exactly these first three
   117	argument vectors, once per operation:
   118	
   119	```text
   120	[<resolved-go>, "telemetry", "off"]
   121	[<resolved-go>, "version"]
   122	[<resolved-go>, "env", "-json", "GOROOT", "GOHOSTOS", "GOHOSTARCH", "GOOS", "GOARCH", "GO386", "GOAMD64", "GOARM", "GOARM64", "GOMIPS", "GOMIPS64", "GOPPC64", "GORISCV64", "GOWASM", "GOTELEMETRY", "GOTELEMETRYDIR"]
   123	```
   124	
   125	The manager requires the probed `GOROOT` to equal the independently resolved
   126	root, normalizes the bounded single-line `go version` output, verifies the
   127	native host and target values, and only then fingerprints the selected tree
   128	using `curator-go-toolchain-v1` as defined by Protocol Core section 8.2.
   129	
   130	For each active build command, in provider-first closure order and then
   131	Unicode-scalar lexical command order within a node, it invokes exactly these
   132	two further argument vectors from the command's canonical `source_dir`:
   133	
   134	```text
   135	[<resolved-go>, "list", "-mod=vendor", "-deps", "-json", "-buildvcs=false", "-compiler=gc", "-pgo=off", "."]
   136	[<resolved-go>, "build", "-mod=vendor", "-trimpath", "-buildvcs=false", "-buildmode=exe", "-compiler=gc", "-pgo=off", "-ldflags=-linkmode=internal -libgcc=none", "-o", <manager-staging-artifact>, "."]
   137	```
   138	
   139	These are the only five Go argument-vector forms. The `-ldflags=...` value and
   140	manager-derived staging path are each one argument. The manager MUST NOT use a
   141	shell, command string, response file, package pattern, package-selected
   142	executable, environment value, argument, tag, flag, output path, build recipe,
   143	hook, plugin, generator, overlay, post-build action, or fallback command. The
   144	first three probes read no package byte and run directly from the parent; the
   145	`go list` and `go build` vectors run inside the worker session of section 2.2.1.
   146	
   147	The bootstrap environment starts empty except for indispensable operating
   148	system process variables. It sets `GOENV=off`, `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, `LC_ALL=C`,
   149	and `LANG=C`, contains no inherited `GOROOT` or target, and sets `GOPATH`,
   150	`GOMODCACHE`, `GOCACHE`, `GOTMPDIR`, `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, `PATH`, and
   151	`TMPDIR` below operation-private roots. `PATH` names a manager-owned empty
   152	directory. On Windows, `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `USERPROFILE`, `TEMP`, and
   153	`TMP` are also private. The manager MUST verify that `GOTELEMETRY` is `off` and
   154	that `GOTELEMETRYDIR` is below the private platform configuration root.
   155	
   156	After the probes, the build environment retains those settings and adds only
   157	the resolved `GOROOT`, native `GOOS` and `GOARCH`, exactly one applicable
   158	trusted architecture-tuning variable returned by the fixed probe, and:
   159	
   160	```text
   161	GO111MODULE=on
   162	GOFLAGS=
   163	GOPROXY=off
   164	GOSUMDB=off
   165	GOPRIVATE=
   166	GONOPROXY=none
   167	GONOSUMDB=none
   168	GOVCS=*:off
   169	GOWORK=off
   170	CGO_ENABLED=0
   171	GO_EXTLINK_ENABLED=0
   172	GOEXPERIMENT=
   173	```
   174	
   175	No ambient or package Go, compiler, assembler, linker, telemetry,
   176	executable-search, workspace, proxy, authentication, or tuning variable may be
   177	inherited. `GOOS` and `GOARCH` MUST equal the probed host target; cross-builds
   178	are unsupported. Module resolution is vendor-only and networkless. The manager
   179	MUST NOT download, tidy, vendor, generate, test, run, install, or fetch a
   180	package, use a workspace or PGO profile, or switch toolchains. A `go.mod`
   181	version or `toolchain` directive that would require switching to an untrusted or
